      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T13:36:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, then it means that using pkvm_hyp-\u003enum_cpus is generally incorrect (since it is num_possible_cpus() i.e. the number of set bits in the bitmask, not the number of the highest set bit, so we may miss some CPUs)?",
      "parentUuid": "415872a8_27088983",
      "revId": "4bd0f47282f690f545327b9580162844e67d0b06",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8542db83_18253664",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/init.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T14:14:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like we can (and should) use `for_each_possible_cpu()` here (like we already use it in some cases in the hypervisor code, e.g. in pkvm_init_finalize()), instead of iterating from 0 to pkvm_hyp-\u003enum_cpus?\n\nAnd then `pkvm_hyp-\u003enum_cpus` becomes unused, and it seems not very useful anyway (and potentially misleading, like in this case), so we might just remove it?",
      "parentUuid": "dea1d69a_48165fa3",
      "revId": "4bd0f47282f690f545327b9580162844e67d0b06",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb6ccaa2_c04c25ae",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/init.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T14:30:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Hmm, then it means that using pkvm_hyp-\u003enum_cpus is generally incorrect (since it is num_possible_cpus() i.e. the number of set bits in the bitmask, not the number of the highest set bit, so we may miss some CPUs)?\n\nIndeed.\n\n\u003e Looks like we can (and should) use for_each_possible_cpu() here (like we already use it in some cases in the hypervisor code, e.g. in pkvm_init_finalize()), instead of iterating from 0 to pkvm_hyp-\u003enum_cpus?\n\nWith that, seems not able to get the vcpu pointer unless:\n1) we assign vcpu pointer in if which is not preferred by the checkpatch.\n2) we expand the for_each_possible_cpu() and assign the vcpu pointer in the for loop.\n\nProbably 2) is better?\n\n\u003e And then pkvm_hyp-\u003enum_cpus becomes unused, and it seems not very useful anyway (and potentially misleading, like in this case), so we might just remove it?\n\nThis is the only place to use pkvm_hyp-\u003enum_cpus, and if this place doesn\u0027t use it, then it makes sense to remove it.",
      "parentUuid": "8542db83_18253664",
      "revId": "4bd0f47282f690f545327b9580162844e67d0b06",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd6a8e10_d8cc021b",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/init.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T17:22:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMHO 2) would be a bit unfortunate: IIUC it would mean hardcoding the implementation details of for_each_possible_cpu() i.e. `for_each_set_bit(cpu, cpumask_bits(mask), small_cpumask_bits)`. Those details may change in upstream in the future, and so on...\n\nSo maybe it\u0027s better to go with 1) and just ignore the checkpatch warning?\n\n...Or alternatively we could do it the other way around: change `pkvm-\u003ehost_vcpus` (and `pkvm-\u003epcpus` as well) to index their elements by consecutive numbers from 0..num_cpus-1 which are not necessarily the same as the CPU numbers. Although that would require a bit more changes (to convert between those indexes and CPU numbers, etc).\n\n...BTW also just a minor note: instead of `pkvm_hyp-\u003ehost_vcpus[(i)]` we could use `per_cpu(host_vcpu, (cpu))` here?",
      "parentUuid": "bb6ccaa2_c04c25ae",
      "revId": "4bd0f47282f690f545327b9580162844e67d0b06",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52cc9f87_0d6c6606",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/init.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T18:27:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just quickly tried this, seems to work:\n\n```\n--- a/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/init.h\n+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/init.h\n@@ -41,17 +41,17 @@ bool pkvm_cpu_initialized(int cpu);\n \n /**\n  * for_each_pkvm_initialized_cpu - iterate over initialized pKVM host vCPUs\n- * @i: iterator variable for vCPU index\n+ * @cpu: iterator variable for physical CPU index\n  * @vcpu: struct kvm_vcpu pointer to host vCPU, assigned by macro.\n  *\n  * Iterates over all host vCPUs in the pkvm_hyp-\u003ehost_vcpus[] array, skipping\n  * NULL entries and the ones which corresponding CPU is not initialized by\n  * pkvm_init().\n  */\n-#define for_each_pkvm_initialized_cpu(i, vcpu)\t\t\t\t\t\\\n-\tfor ((i) \u003d 0; (i) \u003c pkvm_hyp-\u003enum_cpus \u0026\u0026\t\t\t\t\\\n-\t\t      ({ (vcpu) \u003d pkvm_hyp-\u003ehost_vcpus[(i)]; true; }); (i)++)\t\\\n-\t\tif (!(vcpu) || !pkvm_cpu_initialized((vcpu)-\u003ecpu))\t\t\\\n+#define for_each_pkvm_initialized_cpu(cpu, vcpu)\t\t\t\t\\\n+\tfor_each_possible_cpu(cpu)\t\t\t\t\t\t\\\n+\t\tif (WARN_ON_ONCE(!((vcpu) \u003d per_cpu(host_vcpu, (cpu)))) ||\t\\\n+\t\t    !pkvm_cpu_initialized(cpu))\t\t\t\t\t\\\n \t\t\tcontinue;\t\t\t\t\t\t\\\n \t\telse\n \n```",
      "parentUuid": "bd6a8e10_d8cc021b",
      "revId": "4bd0f47282f690f545327b9580162844e67d0b06",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cbb230e0_0ce1f278",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/init.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-08T01:42:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e ...BTW also just a minor note: instead of pkvm_hyp-\u003ehost_vcpus[(i)] we could use per_cpu(host_vcpu, (cpu)) here?\n\nYes, we could use `per_cpu(host_vcpu, (cpu))`. Actually we were using this at https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4018593/1/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/ept.c#202, And if we decide to ignore the checkpatch warning, we can use the above code.\n\n\u003e...Or alternatively we could do it the other way around: change pkvm-\u003ehost_vcpus (and pkvm-\u003epcpus as well) to index their elements by consecutive numbers from 0..num_cpus-1 which are not necessarily the same as the CPU numbers. Although that would require a bit more changes (to convert between those indexes and CPU numbers, etc).\n\nThis may be something worth to do? As we already have a per_cpu way to get the corresponding pcpu and host_vcpu, which represents index pcpu/host_vcpu via CPU id, then seems no need to use CPU id to index them again in the array. With changing the array index to the consecutive numbers from 0..num_cpus - 1, we will have both ways in the pKVM. There will be more changes, but it may not be complex, as we only need to handle the cases before deprivilege. I can prepare a separate patch for this and we can review to see if it is necessary or not.",
      "parentUuid": "52cc9f87_0d6c6606",
      "revId": "4bd0f47282f690f545327b9580162844e67d0b06",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
